Root cause found. In `_rebuildAllRequests`, the running cumulative is discarded:

```dart
for (var i = 0; i < facts.length; i++) {
  _reqPositions[facts[i]] = i;
  _foldRequestNumber(i, facts[i], null);   // ← always null, return value discarded
}
```

Each fact folds against `null`, so cumulative = own usage only. This is exactly the path `appendAll` (the CLI `trajectory cost` path) takes — my repro shows `appendAll` producing `cum=120/120/null/240` instead of `120/240/240/480`. The live-tail path masked it because later suffix rebuilds thread the cumulative correctly. Let me verify the one-line fix:

